    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0234" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60d2/1a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pearson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-29T17:00:00-05:00">January 29, 1927—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Instruction No. 81, August 16, 1923.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d115-f1"/> Ascertain
                    if negotiation of Treaty of Friendship Commerce and Consular Rights can be
                    expedited. Report promptly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d115-f1" n="1" xml:id="d115-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted a draft treaty of friendship and commerce which had
                    been submitted to the Finnish Government through its Legation in Washington. The
                    draft was similar to that transmitted to the Ambassador in Spain, May 18, 1923,
                        <ref target="frus1923v02#pg_831"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1923, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p.
                        831</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
